    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d643">

                <pb facs="0678" n="666" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg666"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/9274: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Phillips</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-03-24T15:00:00+02:00">March 24, 1941—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 24—11:58 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>399. My 384, March 19, and 396, March 22.<anchor n="51" xml:id="d643-f1"/> With
                    regard to the Albanian campaign our information is to the effect that the
                    Germans have given Mussolini “one more chance” to carry on his campaign against
                    the Greeks and that another Italian offensive will be launched shortly.
                    Mussolini who is now in Rome will return to Albania some time this week. With
                    regard to Cirenaica, we hear that between 4 and 5 German divisions have already
                    landed in Libya and that the <pb facs="0679" n="667" xml:id="pg667"/> German
                    offensive against Cirenaica will be launched within 10 days or 2 weeks.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
